page DatabaseTransactionsPage
  Section id:"database-transactions-introduction" py:{ xs:6 md:10 }
    Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:"1fr auto" } gap:5 align:"end"
      Grid columns:1 gap:3
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "SERVER / DATABASE / TRANSACTIONS"
        Title size:{ xs:"3xl" md:"6xl" } weight:"black"
          "Transactions"
        Text size:"lg" color:"muted"
          "A Dowe Database transaction commits all staged inserts through one checksummed WAL boundary. Local development and the remote Dowe provider share the same atomic commit path."
      Button href:"/docs/server/db" variant:"ghost" scheme:"muted" size:"sm"
        "Database overview"
  Section id:"database-transactions-example" p:{ xs:5 md:7 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "TRANSACTION"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Stage inserts, then publish one result"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "query result db:db.tx opens the transaction. Every nested insert is validated before the WAL frame is written. commit value:room returns the selected inserted record after the durable commit succeeds."
      Code:
        language:"dowe"
        variant:"soft"
        scheme:"surface"
        copyLabel:"Copy Dowe"
        copiedLabel:"Copied"
        content:"""
          handler seedClinicData
            database db provider:"dowe" host:env.DOWE_HOST port:env.DOWE_PORT account:env.DOWE_USER secret:env.DOWE_PASSWORD name:"clinic"
            query result db:db.tx
              query room db:db.insert table:"rooms" value:{ name:"Room 1" status:"available" }
              query doctor db:db.insert table:"staff" value:{ name:"Ada" role:"doctor" }
              commit value:room
            return json:{ ok:true data:result }
        """
  Section id:"database-transactions-guarantees" py:{ xs:7 md:10 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "GUARANTEES"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Durable before visible"
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:2 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"primary" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Atomic commit"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "A conflict or invalid later insert rejects the entire transaction. No earlier staged insert becomes visible or remains as a partial commit."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Durable WAL"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Each transaction has a framed payload, SHA-256 checksum, commit marker, and disk sync. Recovery ignores an incomplete tail and rejects committed corruption."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Snapshot and conflicts"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "MVCC keeps transaction reads on their starting version. A write to a record changed after that version fails with TransactionConflict."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Concurrent group commit"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Concurrent commits may share one disk sync, while retaining separate WAL frames, results, conflict checks, and transaction versions."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Live secondary indexes"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Secondary indexes update in commit order and rebuild from the compacted snapshot plus WAL during recovery, without a full index rewrite per insert."
  Section id:"database-transactions-scope" p:{ xs:5 md:7 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "SCOPE AND OPERATIONS"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Use Dowe provider handles"
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:3 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Local and remote"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Development uses the embedded engine. Production provider:dowe sends the transaction over the authenticated WebSocket protocol."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Insert stage"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "The current Dowe Source Format transaction body accepts insert children. Update, delete, and custom SQL do not participate in this transaction form."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"warning" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Provider boundary"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "PostgreSQL and D1 handles reject db:<handle>.tx during compilation. Their individual operations still use their provider adapters."
  Section id:"database-transactions-operations" py:{ xs:7 md:10 }
    Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:2 } gap:4
      Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
        Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
          "Rollback"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "rollback discards every staged insert without writing a WAL frame. An empty transaction also performs no write."
      Card variant:"soft" scheme:"warning" p:5 rounded:"md"
        Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
          "Lost response"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "Write requests are never retried automatically. If a connection drops after the server commits but before the response arrives, reconcile with a client-supplied ULID or another business idempotency key before retrying."
      Card variant:"soft" scheme:"warning" p:5 rounded:"md"
        Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
          "At-rest boundary"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "Unix storage uses private directory and file modes. WAL checksums detect corruption but do not encrypt records; sensitive deployments still need an encrypted volume and operating-system access controls."
